# StreamDQ Master Rules — Single Source of Truth

This file is the **only rule file** for the StreamDQ project. All other rule files are deprecated.

---

## SECTION 1: PROJECT IDENTITY

**StreamDQ** = "A Context-Aware Framework for Streaming Data Quality Monitoring"

- Validates streaming data quality in real-time with context-aware thresholds and full explainability.
- **NOT** a batch tool. **NOT** a ML anomaly detection system. **NOT** a production-grade product.
- **IS** a research & education platform.

**Tech stack**: Python 3.10+, Apache Spark Structured Streaming, Kafka, SQLite/PostgreSQL, Prometheus, Grafana, dbt.
**Data sources**: NYC TLC Yellow Taxi (replayed), NYC MTA Bus GTFS-realtime (live, public).
**Rule taxonomy**: SYN (syntactic), SEM (semantic), CRS (cross-record).
**10 rules**: SYN001, SYN002, SYN003, SEM001, SEM002, SEM003, GTFSSem002, CRS001, CRS002, CRS003.

**Streaming Engine**: Apache Flink (migrated from Spark).
**Dataset constraint**: CRS001/CRS002 require GPS coordinates — evaluated on NYC MTA Bus GTFS-realtime only. NYC TLC has no GPS (zone-level only).
**CRS rules**: **MUST be implemented in Java** (PyFlink serialization overhead). Not optional.

