## SECTION 3: SCIENTIFIC HONESTY

### SH1 — Every Claim Needs a Citation
Every factual claim needs a citation (DOI/URL). Every result needs implementation + tests + reproducibility doc. **Do NOT** write "X%" without noting it needs measurement or citing a source.

### SH2 — Acknowledge Uncertainty
Say "uncertain about X, reason: Y, suggest verification." **Do NOT** hallucinate data or results.

### SH3 — Three Tiers of Claims
Every claim must be classified:
- **Tier 1 — Verified**: Code inspection, prior published results, established domain knowledge
- **Tier 2 — Estimated** (note: needs measurement): "82% recall" — mark as ESTIMATED, not verified
- **Tier 3 — Unmeasurable** (cite bug/limitation): CRS003 recall — duplicate injection broken

### SH4 — Fabricated Metrics Are Forbidden
PURGE immediately: "94.2%", "13x GE", "91.8%", "245K events/sec", etc. Mark as TIER-2 or TIER-3.

### SH5 — Know the Known Blockers
These documented issues must NOT be re-discovered:
| ID | Blocker | Status |
|----|---------|--------|
| B1 | SYN001 NaN silent pass-through (no `math.isnan()` guard) | Fixed in code |
| B2 | Duplicate injection no-op (CRS003 recall unmeasurable) | Needs proper fix |
| B3 | CRS002 speed range gap (2-20 km/h moderate spoofing) | Known limitation |
| B4 | `foreachBatch` driver bottleneck | **N/A — Flink has no foreachBatch** |
| B5 | SQLite no WAL mode | Known limitation |
| B6 | `processing_latency_ms` hardcoded to 0 | Fixed in Flink (event-time timers) |

### SH6 — Verified vs. Estimated vs. Unmeasurable
- **Verified**: SYN001-003 on synthetic data with known ground truth
- **Estimated**: 82% recall, 85% precision, P99=890ms — all need real benchmark runs
- **Unmeasurable**: CRS003 recall — duplicate injection is broken

