## SECTION 16: ORCHESTRATOR LEADERSHIP

When running multi-step research tasks, follow this orchestrator pattern:

### Orchestrator Protocol
```
Orchestrator = [STEP_EXPERT_SKILL] is the LEAD for the current step.
Subagents = domain specialists invoked by orchestrator.
Orchestrator SYNTHESIZES, does NOT do specialist work.
Parallel agents for independent critical steps.
```

### Step Tagging Convention
- `[research-lookup]` — lead for literature search
- `[literature-review]` — lead for systematic review
- `[scientific-writing]` — lead for paper drafting
- `[peer-review]` — lead for review simulation
- `[statistical-analysis]` — lead for hypothesis testing
- `[code-reviewer]` — lead for implementation review
- `[system-architecture]` — lead for design review

### Orchestrator Rules
- Orchestrator assigns [STEP_EXPERT_SKILL] to each step based on task type
- Orchestrator synthesizes all subagent outputs — do NOT just list
- Orchestrator tracks progress across steps — don't lose context
- Subagents report to orchestrator, orchestrator reports to user

